# canonical: gitignore core + opentofu/core + opentofu/lockfiles-committed @ 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567 — governed region, do not edit
# ╭───═══◎◎◎═══───
# 🏗️ **Local build and test outputs**
# Generated build, test, and cache trees, matched at the workspace root and at every nested depth so single projects and monorepos share one rule.
# ╰───═══◎◎◎═══───
#
# .build/ — what: local build scratch tree; produced by: local build tooling; used by: the build run itself; why ignored: machine-local scratch state that never becomes committed truth.
.build/
# dist/ — what: final distribution output; produced by: build and packaging pipelines; used by: release steps reading it from disk; why ignored: generated output, delivered as published artifacts instead of source.
dist/
# coverage/ — what: test-coverage output trees; produced by: coverage runners of every language; used by: coverage reporters and CI annotations; why ignored: generated measurement output.
coverage/
# .cache/ — what: tool cache trees; produced by: build and test tools; used by: the same tools on this machine; why ignored: regenerable cache state, matched at every depth for monorepo packages.
.cache/

# ╭───═══◎◎◎═══───
# 📤 **Universal toolchain output suffix**
# The one output extension every toolchain in the fleet shares, whatever produces it.
# ╰───═══◎◎◎═══───
#
# *.out — what: generic compiled output files; produced by: compilers and test binaries across toolchains; used by: the invoking process only; why ignored: transient output with no committed role.
*.out

# ╭───═══◎◎◎═══───
# 🖥️ **Editor and operating-system state**
# State files that editors and operating systems leave inside repositories.
# ╰───═══◎◎◎═══───
#
# .DS_Store — what: Finder metadata file; produced by: macOS Finder on folder access; used by: nothing but the local machine; why ignored: operating-system droppings carry no project meaning.
.DS_Store
# .idea/ — what: JetBrains project state tree; produced by: JetBrains IDEs on project open; used by: the local IDE session; why ignored: editor state is personal, not project truth.
.idea/

# ╭───═══◎◎◎═══───
# 🔐 **Never-commit secret-artifact guard**
# The client-side projection of the server-side push boundary; the family set is fixed by the home's canonical secret families and every member is proven present by the render.
# ╰───═══◎◎◎═══───
#
# .env — what: environment variable file carrying secrets and configuration; produced by: developers and dotenv tooling; used by: the application at startup through dotenv loaders; why ignored: secret-bearing local config must never be committed.
.env
# .env.* — what: mode-specific environment files such as .env.production; produced by: developers and deployment tooling; used by: dotenv loaders selecting a mode; why ignored: same secret-bearing family as .env.
.env.*
# .envrc — what: direnv entry file exporting shell variables; produced by: direnv users; used by: direnv on directory entry; why ignored: machine-local shell environment that can export secrets.
.envrc
# .env*.local — what: local overrides of environment files; produced by: developers for personal settings; used by: dotenv loaders after the base file; why ignored: personal local secrets.
.env*.local
# credentials — what: plain credential file at the repository root; produced by: cloud and service CLI login flows; used by: those CLIs for authentication; why ignored: raw credential material.
credentials
# credentials.* — what: credential variants and stores; produced by: CLI login flows; used by: the same CLIs; why ignored: raw credential material in every spelling.
credentials.*
# *.pem — what: PEM-encoded key and certificate material; produced by: openssl and infrastructure tooling; used by: TLS clients and signers; why ignored: private key material.
*.pem
# *.key — what: private key files; produced by: key generators; used by: signers and TLS endpoints; why ignored: private key material.
*.key
# *.p12 — what: PKCS#12 keystore bundles; produced by: certificate export tooling; used by: Windows and Java keystore consumers; why ignored: bundles contain private keys.
*.p12
# *.pfx — what: PKCS#12 export files; produced by: certificate export tooling; used by: Windows credential consumers; why ignored: bundles contain private keys.
*.pfx
# *.jks — what: Java keystore files; produced by: keytool; used by: JVM TLS and signing tooling; why ignored: contains private keys.
*.jks
# *.keystore — what: generic keystore files; produced by: JVM and client tooling; used by: the consuming runtime; why ignored: contains private keys.
*.keystore
# *.kdbx — what: KeePass secret databases; produced by: password managers; used by: the manager application; why ignored: encrypted vault material never belongs in a repository.
*.kdbx
# *.ppk — what: PuTTY private key files; produced by: PuTTYgen; used by: PuTTY-based clients; why ignored: private key material.
*.ppk
# *.gpg — what: GPG key or encrypted secret files; produced by: gpg; used by: gpg consumers; why ignored: key material and encrypted secrets.
*.gpg

# opentofu/core
# ╭───═══◎◎◎═══───
# 🧯 **OpenTofu engine-local surfaces**
# Provider install trees, engine configuration, and crash output of the OpenTofu/Terraform engine.
# ╰───═══◎◎◎═══───
#
# **/.terraform/ — what: downloaded provider and module trees; produced by: tofu init; used by: the engine at plan and apply time; why ignored: regenerable binary provider state, matched at every depth because modules nest their own trees.
**/.terraform/
# .terraformrc — what: user-level engine configuration; produced by: the operator or CI setup; used by: the tofu CLI; why ignored: machine-local configuration that can carry credentials.
.terraformrc
# terraform.rc — what: Windows-named engine configuration; produced by: the operator or CI setup; used by: the tofu CLI on Windows; why ignored: machine-local configuration.
terraform.rc
# crash.log — what: engine crash report; produced by: a crashing tofu run; used by: bug reports when filed manually; why ignored: incident droppings that can embed state.
crash.log
# crash.*.log — what: rotated engine crash reports; produced by: crashing tofu runs; used by: manual bug filing; why ignored: incident droppings.
crash.*.log

# ╭───═══◎◎◎═══───
# 🗄️ **Infrastructure state**
# Real-infrastructure state and plan output; secret-shaped and additionally blocked at the server-side push boundary.
# ╰───═══◎◎◎═══───
#
# *.tfstate — what: infrastructure state file; produced by: tofu apply; used by: the engine as its only truth of what exists; why ignored: contains resource attributes and secrets, server-side blocked as well.
*.tfstate
# *.tfstate.* — what: state backups and lock artifacts; produced by: tofu state operations; used by: recovery runs; why ignored: same secret shape as the state itself.
*.tfstate.*
# *.tfplan — what: saved execution plan binary; produced by: tofu plan -out; used by: tofu apply; why ignored: generated plan data that can embed secrets.
*.tfplan

# ╭───═══◎◎◎═══───
# 🧷 **Instance bindings**
# Per-instance variable and override surfaces whose values are governed in the instance lane, not in module repositories.
# ╰───═══◎◎◎═══───
#
# *.tfvars — what: variable binding files; produced by: operators and CI injection; used by: tofu plan and apply; why ignored: instance values are governed elsewhere and often carry credentials.
*.tfvars
# *.tfvars.json — what: JSON variable binding files; produced by: operators and CI injection; used by: tofu plan and apply; why ignored: instance values governed elsewhere.
*.tfvars.json
# override.tf — what: implicit override module; produced by: local experimentation; used by: the engine automatically whenever present; why ignored: silent local overrides break reviewable infrastructure.
override.tf
# override.tf.json — what: JSON implicit override module; produced by: local experimentation; used by: the engine automatically; why ignored: silent local overrides break reviewable infrastructure.
override.tf.json
# *_override.tf — what: named override files; produced by: local experimentation; used by: the engine automatically; why ignored: silent local overrides break reviewable infrastructure.
*_override.tf
# *_override.tf.json — what: named JSON override files; produced by: local experimentation; used by: the engine automatically; why ignored: silent local overrides break reviewable infrastructure.
*_override.tf.json

# opentofu/lockfiles-committed
# ╭───═══◎◎◎═══───
# 📦 **Lockfile policy: committed**
# A policy statement fragment binding the decision that OpenTofu lock files are committed; it therefore carries no ignore pattern.
# ╰───═══◎◎◎═══───
#
# **/.terraform.lock.hcl — what: dependency lock file pinning provider versions and checksums; produced by: tofu init; used by: every later plan and apply for reproducible provider selection; why ignored: not ignored — committing it is the policy this fragment binds.

